        arc:
          'Boo travels from monster to neighbor without ever saying more than a sentence. For most of the book he exists only as the children’s invention, the malevolent phantom blamed for every stealthy small crime in Maycomb, and their whole summer game is built on him. The gifts, the blanket, and the mended trousers accumulate quietly on the other side of the ledger until Halloween night, when the phantom steps out of the shadows and becomes the person who saves their lives. Scout finally sees him as Arthur and walks him home on her arm, and the transformation is complete: the town’s ghost turns out to have been its gentlest inhabitant.',
